course: dictionary
lesson: 426
title: Words for water on the move
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Read the words around a new word to find its meaning. «Romans were great engineers, building aqueducts for water, arches, domes and concrete.» Aqueducts are built, like arches and domes, and they are for water.
explain: «Aqueducts carried fresh water from hills to cities, sometimes over high stone bridges.» The water travels a long way, and sometimes it crosses over bridges. So an aqueduct is a bridge or channel that carries water.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The Romans built a water bridge to carry fresh water to their cities.» It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
fact: An aqueduct is a man-made bridge, channel or pipe that carries water a long way.
fact: The word comes from Latin: aqua means water, and ducere means to lead.
fact: Romans built famous stone aqueducts with tall arches to bring fresh water to their cities.
fact: The Pont du Gard in France is a famous Roman aqueduct.
fact: Aqueducts use gravity: water flows gently downhill, so the channel must slope slightly.
exercise: «Romans were great engineers, building aqueducts for water, arches, domes and concrete.» What is an aqueduct? | A kind of small boat | *A channel or bridge that carries water | A type of Roman coin | A tall tower for watching the sea
exercise: «Aqueducts carried fresh water from hills to cities, sometimes over high stone bridges.» What helps the water move along an aqueduct? | *A gentle downhill slope | Pumps working all night | Children pushing it uphill | Strong winds blowing from behind
exercise: «Romans were great engineers, building aqueducts for water, arches, domes and concrete.» Find and copy one word from this sentence that means a curved stone support. | concrete | engineers | water | *arches
test: Canal aqueducts like Pontcysyllte in Wales let what cross valleys? | *Boats | Trains | Clouds | Cows
test: Which of these is a good meaning for aqueduct in the sentence «Aqueducts carried fresh water from hills to cities»? | A stone wall around a city | *A channel or bridge that carries water a long way | A hill with a flat top | A type of storm
exam: Which sentence uses aqueduct correctly? | The aqueduct is a loud bird that sings at night | *The Roman aqueduct carried water over the valley to the city | The aqueduct was a sweet pudding served with cream | Our aqueduct went swimming at the seaside
